# DayFlow — Intelligent HR Command Center

## Core Principle

```
DATA → INTELLIGENCE → PRIORITY → RECOMMENDATION → HUMAN DECISION
```

AI supports HR decisions. It never makes irreversible employment decisions. Use explainable terms: **Attendance Anomaly**, **Workplace Risk Signal**, **Workload Signal**, **Leave Pattern**, **HR Recommendation**. Never claim medical/psychological diagnosis, guaranteed resignation, or automatic punishment.

---

## Architecture

```
frontend/  ──REST/JWT──▶  backend/  ──import──▶  ai-engine/
                              │                      │
                              └────import──▶  analytics/
                              │
                              └────PostgreSQL (database/)
```

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `frontend/` | React SPA — UI only; calls backend REST APIs |
| `backend/` | FastAPI — auth, RBAC, business logic, data access |
| `ai-engine/` | ML (Isolation Forest) + Gemini — server-side only |
| `analytics/` | KPIs, trends, HR priority queue |
| `database/` | Schema (`schema.sql`), seed data |
| `docs/` | Architecture, API contract, git workflow |

Frontend never touches PostgreSQL or Gemini directly. Backend is the sole HTTP entry point.

---

## Technology Stack

| Layer | Stack |
|-------|-------|
| Frontend | React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, React Router, Axios, Recharts, Lucide React |
| Backend | Python, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL, Pydantic, JWT, bcrypt |
| AI/ML | Google Gemini API, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, Isolation Forest |
| DevOps | Git, GitHub, Docker |

Environment variables via `.env` (never committed). Use `.env.example` for templates.

